{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791700442,"nonce":"GXMeshmhWLKjRfn8ty+I3oG3KY0=","title":"Vite plugin bundles the SDK, overrides an app's outDir, and compiles TypeScript declarations as CSS","message":"Found while building one small app (a Host, a compiled .css import) with each bundler to document the recipes:\n\n- Vite: a build of the blinc environment bundled blinc_ts itself (43 modules) when the package resolves outside node_modules, as a linked or workspace install does; the bundle then looked for native/blinc_ts.node beside itself and failed. blinc() now marks blinc_ts external in its environment (dev and build).\n- Vite: blinc()'s config hook returned build.outDir 'dist/native', which won over the app's own environments.blinc.build.outDir. Its build defaults now fill in only what the app leaves out.\n- rollup with @rollup/plugin-typescript: blincCss resolves an import through the other plugins first, and TypeScript's resolver answers './card.css' with card.d.css.ts, so the declarations were compiled as CSS (\"expected { after declare const sheet\"). blincCss maps a .d.css.ts answer back to its sheet.\n\nVerified by hand (scratch project): esbuild 0.25+ with a compileCss onLoad plugin, rollup 4 with @rollup/plugin-typescript and blincCss, rolldown 1.2 with blincCss, Vite 8 with blinc() and blincCss() building the blinc environment only; each built app ran. tsc alone compiles but Node cannot import .css, so a tsc-only app adds CSS text at run time.\n\nTests: tests/native-vite-css.mjs builds an app in the blinc environment (own outDir, blinc_ts imported not bundled, runs) and checks blincCss's resolveId against a TypeScript-style answer. Each fix's removal fails it.","files":null}]}